 result←object New arg;parent;name;where;newobj;props;border;nocaption;∆where;∆caption;∆border;client
 (parent name)←object ⍝ Separate non-standard two-part argument
 (∆where ∆caption ∆border)←arg ##._supp.GetInitialProps'where' 'caption' '←border' ⍝ Which of our defaults are they giving us anyway (so we can skip our defaults)

 ⍝? Is where supposed to be centered on the screen? If so, can we use New.Center in some way?
  ⍝ Optionally prepend object defaults (in reverse order) to be handled
 :If 4≠≢∊∆where
     where←,parent._size÷⍤1⊢2 2⍴4 4 2 2 ⍝ Default APL+Win Form size and position ⍝? Does this give us the right data for scale=0? even inverted?
     arg,⍨←⊂'where'where ⍝ [2] Start us with a default 'where' size and position (APL+Win measure) -- will usually be overridden later
 :EndIf
 arg,⍨←(~arg ##._supp.HasInitialProps'caption')/⊂'caption'name ⍝ [1] Use the object name as a default caption
 border←+/∆border,(0=≢∆border)/_border ⍝ Assume default, and handle multi-bit borders

 props←'Form'('Visible' 0)
 nocaption←∆caption≡'' ⍝ (This won't match a ⍬ default, thus it's been provided to us this way)
 :If nocaption∧16>+/border ⍝ No border; no title bar
     props,←('Sizeable' 0)('Moveable' 0)('SysMenu' 0)('MinButton' 0)('MaxButton' 0)('Border' 0)
 :ElseIf nocaption∧1∊border ⍝ Thin border; no title bar
     props,←('Sizeable' 0)('Moveable' 0)('SysMenu' 0)('MinButton' 0)('MaxButton' 0)('Border' 1)
 :Else ⍝ Normal border and title bar
     props,←(16 32 64∊border),¨⍨⊂¨'SysMenu' 'MinButton' 'MaxButton'
     props,←('Sizeable' 1)('Moveable' 1)('Border' 1)
 :EndIf

 newobj←⎕VGET(parent⍕⍛,'.',name)##.##.∆WC props ⍝ Create the actual Dyalog object
 result←parent newobj ##.##.New.Initialize arg ⍝ Complete standard class-initialization procedure (including the hidden _mdi child)

 props←'MDIClient'('Coord' 'RealPixel')('Posn' 0 0)('Size'(newobj ##.##.∆WG'Size'))
 client←⎕VGET(newobj⍕⍛,'._mdi')##.##.∆WC props
 ##.##.New.InitChild newobj client
⍝ The Dyalog MDIClient defaults to occupying the entirety of the parent Form,
⍝ but adjustments may be made to reserve space for other objects to be added within the Form.
⍝ The Attach property is automatically set to stay the same size as the container, unless 'clientwhere' is used to override it
